# Normalise line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf gives the working tree CRLF on Windows while git stores LF. That is mostly
# harmless, but it makes gofmt disagree with CI — gofmt reads the working tree and sees
# CRLF, while the Linux runner checks out LF and is happy. Worse, a shell script or
# container entrypoint checked out with CRLF fails at runtime with an error that names the
# wrong thing entirely.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree makes local checks and CI agree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.bundle binary
